50\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization\n- 2025 GAAP R&D: $1.016B [Actual]; 2024: $0.731B [Actual]; 2023: \u2248$0.691B [Estimate derived from Rev \u2212 COGS \u2212 SG&A \u2212 OpInc]; 2022: \u2248$0.442B [Estimate]\n- 4-yr amortization \u2248 $0.720B [Assumption]\n- Adjusted operating income = $0.619B + $1.016B \u2212 $0.720B = $0.915B [Estimate]\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC Treatment\n- FY2025 SBC: $0.218B [Actual]. Adjusted owner FCF = OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC = $0.783 \u2212 $0.034 \u2212 $0.218 = $0.531B [Arithmetic]. SBC is NOT added back in this analysis.\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization\n- FY2025 operating leases $0.471B present value [Actual \u2014 Section 6B]. Minor; not added to net debt because the company holds $2.5B liquidity and no debt.\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data Asset Valuation\n- Not quantified \u2014 niche CNS brands have less transferable brand value. [Unconfirmed] \u2014 no reliable Interbrand-style figure for NBIX brands.\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC\n- Adjusted NOPAT: $0.915B \u00d7 0.79 = $0.723B [Estimate]\n- Adjusted invested capital: reported IC \u2248 $1.125B (equity $3.253B + debt $0.415B \u2212 cash/investments $2.543B) + unamortized R&D \u2248 $2.16B = $3.285B\n- Adjusted ROIC \u2248 22.0% [Estimate]; GAAP ROIC \u2248 43% [Estimate]; gap >5pp explained by R&D expensing and cash distortion. Both confirm HIGH quality.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett)\nOwner Earnings (2025) = NI $0.479B + D&A $0.030B \u2212 maintenance capex $0.034B \u2212 \u0394WC (\u2212$0.015B) = $0.490B [Estimate]\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 0-1/0-2. Archetype & Engine Selection\n- Archetype: B \u2014 Quality Compounder\n  (1) 3 consecutive years of GAAP profitability; (2) FCF margin ~26%; (3) ROIC > WACC for 5+ years; (4) revenue growth 20%+ but with durable products, not option value).\n- Engine 1 (Traditional DCF + Multiples).\n- If Engine 4 (Option-Led) were used instead, it would over-weight the 2027 Phase 3 binaries and under-weight the already-commercial base \u2014 base rates for Phase 3 success (~35\u201340%) do not justify treating pipeline as core value.\n- Not in transition; all criteria for Quality Compounder met.\n\nStep 3-1. WACC Derivation\n- Rf = 4.70% [Actual \u2014 FRED 10Y 2026-08-21]\n- ERP = 4.75% [Assumption \u2014 long-run historical/implied range]\n- Beta = 0.85 [Assumption \u2014 vendor 0.394 is on an unstated window and is inconsistent with a mid-cap growth biopharma; normalized 0.75\u20131.0. Unlevered pharma base rate ~0.65, levered with pipeline optionality \u2192 0.85]\n- Cost of equity = 4.70% + 0.85 \u00d7 4.75% = 8.74%\n- WACC = 8.74% \u2248 8.7% (all-equity; no debt, net cash addressed at equity bridge)\n\nStep 3-2. Explicit Forecast (all $B; fiscal years)\n| FY | Revenue | OpMargin | EBIT | NOPAT(21%) | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | Owner FCF |\n|----|---------|----------|------|-----------|-----|-------|-----|-----------|\n| 2026E | 3.85 | 29.1% | 1.121 | 0.886 | 0.100 | 0.050 | 0.150 | 0.786 |\n| 2027E | 4.58 | 30.5% | 1.397 | 1.104 | 0.120 | 0.060 | 0.110 | 1.054 |\n| 2028E | 5.22 | 31.0% | 1.618 | 1.278 | 0.150 | 0.065 | 0.096 | 1.267 |\n| 2029E | 5.04 | 30.0% | 1.512 | 1.194 | 0.180 | 0.070 | \u22120.027 | 1.331 |\n| 2030E | 4.86 | 29.0% | 1.409 | 1.113 | 0.200 | 0.075 | \u22120.027 | 1.265 |\n| 2031E | 4.36 | 28.5% | 1.243 | 0.982 | 0.220 | 0.080 | \u22120.075 | 1.197 |\n| 2032E | 3.83 | 28.0% | 1.072 | 0.847 | 0.240 | 0.085 | \u22120.079 | 1.081 |\nTerminal: g = 2.5% [Assumption \u2014 long-run nominal GDP]; Terminal FCF = 1.081\u00d71.025 = 1.108; TV = 1.108/(0.087\u22120.025) = $17.87B.\n\nFORECAST SOURCES:\n- 2026 revenue: $3.85B = INGREZZA guidance mid $2.85B [Actual \u2014 Q2 call raised guidance] + CRENESSITY ~$0.73B [Estimate \u2014 Q2 $184M annualizing >$735M; Q1 ~$131M] + VYKAT recognized ~$0.24B [Estimate \u2014 $54M Q2, slower H2 due to discontinuations] + other $0.045B [Actual run-rate]\n- INGREZZA 2027 +10%, 2028 +7% [Assumption \u2014 mgmt: \"continued growth through 2027-2028\"; VMAT2 class growing double-digit]\n- INGREZZA 2029 \u221215% [Assumption \u2014 IRA negotiation implementation 2029 per mgmt; Medicare-heavy TD population]\n- INGREZZA 2030 \u221215%, 2031 \u221230%, 2032 \u221240% [Assumption \u2014 core compound patent expiries 2031\u20132037 (Pharsight); generic valbenazine approved but settlement-limited]\n- CRENESSITY 2027 $1.0B \u2192 2032 $1.80B [Assumption \u2014 Q2 annualized $735M at 15% penetration; 40% penetration by 2032]\n- VYKAT 2027 $0.40B \u2192 2032 $0.95B [Assumption \u2014 blockbuster potential per mgmt; slowed by STAT safety signal (7 deaths, 100+ SAEs unadjudicated)]\n- Op margins 29\u201331% 2026-28, declining to 28% by 2032 [Assumption \u2014 guidance R&D mid $1.225B and SG&A mid $1.388B for 2026 [Actual]; operating leverage then INGREZZA cliff compression]\n- Tax 21% [Assumption \u2014 U.S. statutory; pack withholds effective rate]\n- D&A: $0.10B in 2026 incl. $20M/qtr purchase amortization [Actual \u2014 Q2 call]; rising with VYKAT amortization [Assumption]\n- Capex: $0.05\u20130.085B [Assumption \u2014 1\u20132% of revenue, consistent with history]\n- \u0394WC: 15% of incremental revenue until 2028; then small releases as revenue declines [Assumption \u2014 pharma receivables ~60-70 days; negative WC as shrinking receivables become liquid]\n\nStep 3-3. DCF Result\n- PV(Explicit FCFs) @8.7% mid-year: 0.764 + 0.930 + 1.028 + 0.993 + 0.868 + 0.755 + 0.628 = $5.966B\n- PV(TV) = $17.87B / 1.7226 = $10.37B\n- EV = $16.34B\n- Net cash = +$0.50B [Estimate]\n- Equity = $16.84B\n- Per share = $16.84B / 101.6M = $166 [Estimate]\n\nStep 3-4. Multiple Cross-Check\n- 2026E GAAP EPS \u2248 $8.9 [Estimate]; trailing P/E 22.0\u00d7 [Actual]; forward P/E 17.1\u00d7\n- 2026E non-GAAP EPS \u2248 $9.2 (excl. SBC, amortization, one-time acquisition costs) [Estimate]; forward non-GAAP P/E \u2248 16.6\u00d7\n- Peer set: mid-cap specialty pharma (e.g., ITCI, ACAD, AXSM) trades 12\u201320\u00d7 forward non-GAAP EPS [Assumption]; NBIX at 16.6\u00d7 is near premium due to 25%+ EPS growth \u2192 PEG \u2248 0.7 [Estimate]\n- EV/EBITDA 2026E \u2248 15.0B / (1.121+0.100) = 12.3\u00d7 [Estimate] \u2014 reasonable for the growth rate\n\u2192 Multiple cross-check SUPPORTS the DCF output, no DCF-only conclusion.\n\nStep 3-X. Tornado Sensitivity (Top 3 variables ranked by IV impact)\n1. WACC \u00b11\u03c3 (\u00b10.5pp): IV range $155\u2013$180 \u2192 most important because of long duration\n2. INGREZZA 2029\u201332 decline path: if \u221225%/-25%/-50%/-50% instead of \u221215%/-15%/-30%/-40%, IV falls to \u2248 $145\n3. VYKAT safety outcome: if resolved positively and VYKAT reaches $1B by 2030, IV +$12\u201315\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n1. Competitive Response: A potential CAH competitor was just acquired (per Q2 call). AbbVie (Austedo) competes in VMAT2. In schizophrenia, if direclidine succeeds, BMS (Cobenfy) and AbbVie (emraclidine) will defend. Impact: \u22122 (moderate negative on long-term margins).\n2. Reflexivity: Positive \u2014 the strong stock ($186 high vs $122 low in 52w) enabled the Soleno all-cash deal; SBC attracts talent. Negative \u2014 a sustained de-rating would reduce M&A currency and amplify talent pressure.\n3. Customer Behavior: INGREZZA pays down to 70% Medicare coverage \u2014 payer dependency is structural. CRENESSITY: prescriber base tripled YoY but 15% penetration means early-adopter phase. VYKAT: discontinuations from edema reflect early-adopter cohort; mainstream adoption requires safety resolution.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 4-1/2/3. Scenarios (probabilities sum to 100%)\n- Prior: base rates (Section 1.5) \u2014 Phase 3 CNS success 35\u201340%; orphan safety-signal restriction 30\u201340%; company survival >90%.\n- Update triggers incorporated: (1) Q2 2026 strong beat, INGREZZA guidance RAISED [Actual \u2014 +]; (2) VYKAT safety signal (7 deaths, 100+ SAEs) [Actual \u2014 STAT 2026-08-12] [\u2212]; (3) direclidine Phase 3 initiated/ongoing with 2027 readout [Actual] [neutral]; (4) Q2 cash ~$500M, no debt [Actual] [+].\n\nBEAR \u2014 30% \u2192 $85/share\n- VYKAT: FDA restricts label or risk-mitigation cripples adoption; 2027 sales $150M, declining to $50M by 2032 (write-off of $2.9B deal implied)\n- INGREZZA: IRA 2029 cut \u221225%, generic entry begins 2031 (\u221250% per year)\n- CRENESSITY: peaks at $1.2B (endocrinologist fragmentation)\n- No Phase 3 pipeline contribution\n- FCF path: 0.65 / 0.78 / 0.85 / 0.78 / 0.65 / 0.50 / 0.45\n- PV \u2248 $3.6B + TV $4.3B + net cash 0.5 \u2192 $8.4B \u2192 $83\u201387\n\nBASE \u2014 50% \u2192 $166/share\n- As per DCF in Section 3. VYKAT survives with $0.95B peak; CRENESSITY reaches $1.8B; INGREZZA declines on IRA + patent schedule; pipeline adds $0 in base case.\n- 50% CI: $140\u2013$195 (WACC 8.2\u20139.2%, INGREZZA decline \u00b15pp)\n\nBULL \u2014 20% \u2192 $290/share\n- VYKAT safety resolved as non-causal (7 deaths within background mortality of PWS); drug reaches $1B by 2029\n- Direclidine (schizophrenia) POSITIVE Phase 3 2027; launch 2029; $2B peak by 2032\n- Osavampator (MDD) POSITIVE Phase 3 2027; $1B peak by 2032\n- INGREZZA IRA impact only \u22125% (favourable negotiation outcome)\n- FCF path: 0.79 / 1.15 / 1.60 / 1.95 / 2.30 / 2.60 / 2.75\n- PV \u2248 $8.7B + TV \u2248 $21.1B + 0.5 \u2192 $30.3B \u2192 $298\n\nStep 4-4. Expected Price & MoS\nExpected Price = 0.30(85) + 0.50(166) + 0.20(290) = $166.5\nExpected return vs $152.57 = +9.1%\nMargin of Safety (base case) = (166 \u2212 152.57)/166 = 8.1% \u2192 LIMITED\nExpected MoS (prob.-weighted) = (166.5 \u2212 152.57)/166.5 = 8.4% \u2192 LIMITED\n\nStep 4-5. Probability Calibration Audit\nBull 20% implies joint probability \u2248 20% of BOTH Phase 3 success AND VYKAT clearance. Given base rates ~40% \u00d7 35% \u00d7 60% \u2248 8.4%, 20% is generous but justified by the Cobenfy class validation and Neurocrine's record. Flagged but accepted.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- Market-implied horizon: 22.0\u00d7 trailing P/E on +17% EPS growth implies market is pricing ~3 years of sustained growth with NO INGREZZA terminal decline [Estimate]\n- My horizon: 5\u20136 years, explicitly modelling the 2029 IRA event and 2031\u201332 patent erosion\n- Spread: ~2\u20133 years of forecast horizon advantage\n- Arbitrage exists but is small: the market is already discounting the 2029\u20132032 cliff in the 8% MoS. No significant horizon mispricing.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u255