033 generic entry regardless of Pharsight's \"2040\" estimate.\n3. VYKAT: 7 deaths in a ~1,000-patient launch cohort is a catastrophic safety signal for an orphan metabolic disease. The $2.9B acquisition is at risk of becoming a $2.9B write-down.\n4. R&D expense is 35% of revenue. If Phase 3 fails, the stock faces a double-whammy: pipeline narrative collapse + the realization that R&D spend cannot be cut without strangling future growth.\n5. SG&A grew 22% in 2025 and is guided to +19% in 2026. With 3 launches running simultaneously, margins are capped; any INGREZZA deceleration destroys the operating-leverage story.\n6. At 22\u00d7 trailing P/E, the stock is priced for perfection in a company with two 2027 binary events and one unresolved safety investigation.\n7. CRENESSITY's 15% penetration against a fragmented prescriber base (many treating 1\u20132 patients) means the \"large runway\" is a function of changing endocrinologist behavior, a notoriously slow process.\n\nLogic Combat\n- Long logic strength: 6/10\n- Short logic strength: 7/10\n- Gap < 2 \u2192 CONVICTION DOWNGRADE APPLIED (\u22121 point to effective conviction; final conviction = 8/15)\n\nAdversarial Data\n- STAT News (August 12, 2026) is the highest-quality bear source found; the reporting is sourced to clinicians and FDA's FAERS, not speculative.\n- No Hindenburg-style report located within search budget. [Unconfirmed]\n\nKilled Arguments\n- \"CRENESSITY will grow to $3B\": killed by the 15% penetration being a small patient pool (classic CAH ~15\u201320K US patients); realistic peak $1.8B.\n- \"VYKAT will be a blockbuster by 2028\": killed by the safety signal; pushed to 2029\u20132030 and held at $950M peak.\n- \"Directionally positive Phase 2 \u2192 Phase 3 will succeed\": killed by CNS base rates; bull case requires both assets to beat ~35\u201340% odds.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u