B peak) for an orphan/rare-disease drug: **15\u201325%** (CRENESSITY first-year $301M [Actual] is on the better end of the distribution)\n- $2\u20133B product acquisition earning ROIC > WACC within 5 years: **~30\u201335%** [Estimate]\n- CNS Phase 3 success (psychiatry): MDD adjunct **~50\u201360%**; schizophrenia **~30\u201340%** [Unconfirmed \u2014 my own estimate]\n- Product with 7 FAERS-reported deaths: eventual label restriction or withdrawal **~40\u201360%** [Unconfirmed \u2014 my own estimate]\n- Patent challenge \u2192 generic entry within 2\u20133 years of first Paragraph IV: **30\u201350%** [Unconfirmed]\n\n**Step 1.5-2. Deviation from base rate:** My base case gives NBIX's commercial portfolio a >90% survival base rate and models CRENESSITY as a probable $1.5B peak seller. Justification: (1) INGREZZA is entrenched first-in-class with 22 US patents, none expired [Actual \u2014 GreyB/DrugPatentWatch], (2) CRENESSITY has 2-year Phase 3 data with no competitor [Actual \u2014 company], (3) VYKAT has first-and-only approval in PWS hyperphagia [Actual \u2014 company]. **This justifies base-rate success, not above-base-rate pricing.**\n\n**Step 1.5-3. Base-rate shock check:** The market at $152.57 implies bull-case pipeline success (2 Phase 3 approvals with multi-billion peaks) at probabilities >50% \u2014 that is >1.5x the CNS base rate \u2192 **RED FLAG:** requires exceptional evidence. None available in the pack beyond management assertion. Forecast therefore keeps pipeline optionality out of the base case.\n\nSECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY (Buffett + Lynch)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Step 2-1. Business understanding (3 sentences):** NBIX develops and commercializes first-in-class CNS/endocrine drugs. Current portfolio: INGREZZA (valbenazine \u2014 tardive dyskinesia and Huntington's chorea), CRENESSITY (crinecerfont \u2014 classic congenital adrenal hyperplasia), VYKAT XR (diazoxide choline \u2014 Prader-Willi hyperphagia, acquired with Soleno, May 2026). Pipeline: late-stage osavampator (MDD) and direclidine (schizophrenia) with Phase 3 readouts in 2027. **Understandability: High.**\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat assessment (0\u20133 each):**\n| Moat type | Score | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, patents, IP to 2036\u20132038+) | 3 | Stable/Widening |\n| Switching costs (stabilized patients, physician inertia) | 3 | Stable |\n| Network effects | 0 | \u2014 |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Stable |\n| Economies of scale (specialty sales force) | 2 | Widening |\n| Regulatory/orphan barriers | 3 | Stable |\n| Data moat (real-world safety/efficacy) | 2 | Narrowing for VYKAT; Widening elsewhere |\n| **Total** | **14 / 21** | **Wide moat** \u2014 but VYKAT's safety signal [Actual \u2014 STAT] is narrowing one franchise |\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch classification:** **Fast grower** (3-yr revenue CAGR +22.3% [Actual]). Checkpoint: growth durability hinges on INGREZZA LOE timing [Unconfirmed] \u2014 the core risk.\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial strength scorecard:**\n- Revenue CAGR 5-yr: +22.3% [Actual]; Revenue 3-yr CAGR: ~+16.6% [Arithmetic on FY22\u201325]\n- Operating margin: TTM 21.6%; 11-yr median 9.2% [Actual] \u2192 expanding\n- ROE: 22.1% [Vendor \u2014 Actual]; ROIC est. \u226514% [Assumption]\n- FCF conversion: OCF/NI = 1.27 TTM [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt: cash+marketable securities $482M (6/30/2026) vs operating leases $471M (FY25) \u2192 \u2248 net neutral; $1.0B revolver undrawn [Actual \u2014 company]\n- **Judgment: Excellent** quantitative scorecard; SBC drag is the main quality discount.\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u20133 each):**\nBuyback efficiency 2 (net buyback 2025 but modest); M&A track record 1 (Soleno $2.9B all-cash for a safety-flagged asset [Actual]); Capex efficiency 3 (asset-light; incremental ROIC >20% [Assumption]); Rationality 1 (acquisition consumed most of the $2.54B investment stack [Actual]); Guidance accuracy 3 (2026 INGREZZA guidance raised twice [Actual]). Insider bonus: 0 (insider ownership 1.06% [Vendor]; no cluster signal). **Total: 10/15 \u2014 Good, but the Soleno deal is a red flag in hindsight.**\n\nSECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Step 2.5-1. R&D capitalization:** 2026 GAAP R&D guide $1.275\u20131.325B [Actual]. Capitalizing 5-year amortization: adjust op income +R&D \u2212amortization. Approx. adjustment +$0.5B to EBIT, +$1.5\u20132.0B to invested capital [Assumption]. \n**Step 2.5-2. SBC:** FY2025 SBC $218M (7.6% of revenue) [Actual]. Deduct as cash expense: **Adjusted FCF FY2025 = OCF $783M \u2212 capex $34M \u2212 SBC $218M = $531M** [Arithmetic]. TTM \u2248 $640M [Arithmetic]. The market's non-GAAP EPS adds back SBC; I do not.\n**Step 2.5-3. Operating leases:** $471M (FY25) [Actual] added to debt; net debt \u2248 0.\n**Step 2.5-4. Brand/data:** not material for branded rare-disease drugs; [Unconfirmed] \u2014 skip.\n**Step 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC:** ~12\u201315% [Assumption] vs GAAP ROE 22.1% \u2014 gap explained by expensed R&D and SBC.\n**Step 2.5-6. Owner earnings (Buffett):** FY2025 = NI $479M + D&A $30M \u2212 maintenance capex $35M \u2212 \u0394WC (non-cash) ~$60M \u2212 SBC $218M \u2248 **$197M** [Estimate]. Strong but far below reported FCF.\n\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION ENGINE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Step 0-1/0-2 selection.** NBIX is a **Quality Compounder (Archetype B) in transition toward a Product-Platform Hybrid with a significant Option-Led overlay**. The commercial franchise is profitable and FCF-generative (anchors Engine 1); the 2027 Phase 3 readouts add genuine option value (Engine 4 overlay). Transition evidence: commercial portfolio now 3 products; 2026 revenue \u2248 $3.9B with 3 launches; but pipeline is not yet revenue >50% or FCF-positive on its own. Per 0-3, **Blended Engine = Engine 1 (65%) + Engine 4 (35%)** weighted. If a single engine were forced, Engine 1.\n\n**Forecast \u2014 explicit per-year model (all dollars in $B except per-share):**\n\n| Year | Revenue | EBIT margin | EBIT | nOPAT (21%) | +D&A | \u2212SBC | \u2212Capex | \u2212\u0394WC | FCF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 3.87 | 32.0% | 1.238 | 0.978 | 0.115 | 0.260 | 0.040 | 0.053 | **0.740** |\n| 2027 | 4.42 | 33.5% | 1.481 | 1.170 | 0.120 | 0.290 | 0.050 | 0.028 | **0.922** |\n| 2028 | 4.80 | 34.5% | 1.656 | 1.308 | 0.125 | 0.320 | 0.055 | 0.019 | **1.039** |\n| 2029 | 5.05 | 34.5% | 1.742 | 1.376 | 0.125 | 0.340 | 0.060 | 0.013 | **1.088** |\n| 2030 | 5.00 | 33.0% | 1.650 | 1.304 | 0.130 | 0.340 | 0.060 | (0.003) | **1.037** |\n| 2031 | 4.85 | 30.0% | 1.455 | 1.149 | 0.120 | 0.330 | 0.060 | (0.008) | **0.887** |\n| 2032 | 4.60 | 27.0% | 1.242 | 0.981 | 0.115 | 0.320 | 0.060 | (0.013) | **0.729** |\n| Terminal | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | **0.620** |\n\n**Revenue path (sourced):**\n- INGREZZA: FY25 $2.5B [Actual]; 2026 guided $2.825\u20132.875B [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 release]; 2027 +10%, 2028 +5%, 2029 0%, 2030 \u22125%, 2031\u221232 \u221210%/yr [Assumption \u2014 LOE onset modeled 2031\u201332; patents to 2036 [Unconfirmed], Paragraph IV open since 2025 [Unconfirmed] creates wide uncertainty]\n- CRENESSITY: FY25 $301M [Actual]; 2026 \u2248 $0.74B [Estimate \u2014 Q1 $153M + Q2 $184M + H2; [Actual quarters]]; to $1.6B by 2030 [Assumption \u2014 orphan ramp, IP to 2038 [Actual]]\n- VYKAT XR: 2026 \u2248 $0.25B [Estimate \u2014 $54M partial Q2 + full Q3/Q4 [Actual]; pro-forma $94M/quarter [Actual]]; 2027\u20132030 $0.30\u2192$0.22B [Assumption \u2014 safety-driven deceleration: 7 deaths/100+ SAEs [Actual \u2014 STAT]]\n- Other revenue: ~$0.02B/yr [Actual history]\n\n**Margin path (sourced):** 2026 non-GAAP R&D guide $1.14\u20131.19B; non-GAAP SG&A $1.325\u20131.35B [Actual] \u2192 non-GAAP EBIT \u2248 32% in 2026; expansion to 34.5% by 2029 on operating leverage [Assumption]; contraction 2030\u201332 as INGREZZA erodes [Assumption].\n**SBC:** $218M FY25 [Actual]; $260M FY26 (incl. ~$58M Soleno acceleration [Actual]); ~7% of revenue thereafter [Assumption]. **Treated as cash expense \u2014 deliberate; the pack's warning on OCF-minus-SBC is followed.**\n**Capex:** $34M FY25 [Actual]; $40\u201360M thereafter [Assumption \u2014 asset-light, 1.2% of revenue].\n**\u0394WC:** non-cash WC at ~5% of incremental revenue; releases in decline years [Assumption].\n**D&A:** $30M FY25 + $85\u201390M acquired-intangible amortization 2026 [Actual] \u2192 $115M, rising to $130M [Assumption].\n**Tax rate:** 21% US statutory [Assumption \u2014 pack notes rate not held but identity holds].\n**Discount rate (WACC):** Rf = 4.7% [Actual \u2014 10Y 2026-08-21]; ERP = 4.5% [Assumption]; beta = 0.65 [Assumption \u2014 vendor beta 0.394 is window-unreliable, [Actual-tagged but not consumption-grade]; 0.65 reflects clinical-event idiosyncratic risk]; **CoE = 4.7% + 0.65\u00d74.5% = 7.6%; no debt \u2192 WACC = 7.6%; round to 8.0%** [Assumption \u2014 small-cap/pipeline premium].\n\n**DCF output at 8.0%:**\nExplicit FCF PV (2026\u20132032): $4.79B [Arithmetic]\nTerminal value: $0.620/0.08 = $7.75B; PV = $4.52B [Arithmetic]\nEV = $9.31B; + net cash \u2248 $0.01B (cash+securities $482M post-Soleno [Actual] \u2212 op leases $471M [Actual]; investment-overlap [Unconfirmed])\n**Equity value = $9.32B \u2192 $91.7/share (commercial core, no pipeline).**\n**Pipeline option overlay (Engine 4):** osavampator 50% success \u00d7 $1.0B peak PV \u2248 $0.9B; direclidine 35% \u00d7 $1.5B peak PV \u2248 $1.0B; early pipeline \u2248 $0.2B [All Assumption/Estimate \u2014 weighted for 2028\u201329 launch] \u2192 +$2.1B \u2248 **+$21/share.**\n**\u2192 Intrinsic value, base, pipeline-inclusive: \u2248 $113/share.**\nSensitivity (commercial core): WACC 7% \u2192 +$13/sh; WACC 9% \u2192 \u2212$11/sh; terminal g = 2% \u2192 +$6\u201312/sh; INGREZZA LOE pushed to 2036 \u2192 +$3\u20135/sh.\n\n**Multiples cross-check:** 2027 consensus non-GAAP EPS $10.79 [Estimate \u2014 Zacks]; restoring SBC (~$2.7/sh) \u2192 real EPS \u2248 $8.1 \u2192 at 14\u201315x = $113\u2013121 [Estimate]. Trailing GAAP P/E 22.0x [Vendor]; forward 2026 GAAP EPS \u2248 $5.4 [Assumption] \u2192 28x. EV/EBITDA(2026E) \u2248 15.5/1.355 = 11.4x [Arithmetic]. **Cross-check corroborates $113\u2013125, not $153.**\n**Reverse DCF at T0 $152.57:** requires 2030 revenue \u2248 $7\u20138B with two pipeline approvals and INGREZZA holding to 2036, or WACC \u22646.5%. That is bull-case, not base-case [Assumption].\n**Tornado (top-3 drivers):** (1) INGREZZA LOE timing; (2) VYKAT regulatory outcome; (3) 2027 Phase 3 results.\n\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- **Competitive response:** INGREZZA \u2013 3\u20134 generic filers after 2025 Paragraph IV [Unconfirmed] and 2 other VMAT2 franchises (Austedo) \u2192 price competition post-LOE severe. CRENESSITY \u2013 no near-term competitor; in-licensed alternatives historically failed. VYKAT \u2013 no competitor in PWS hyperphagia, but safety scrutiny suppresses the category. Impact: \u22121 (net).\n- **Reflexivity:** Positive \u2014 strong stock enabled the $2.9B all-cash Soleno deal [Actual]; negative \u2014 a derating would impair M&A currency and SBC attractiveness. Feedback loop real but secondary.\n- **Customer/LTV evolution:** INGREZZA prescriber base mature; CRENESSITY extends from adults to pediatric and now <4yr Phase 2 (initiated [Actual]); VYKAT's VAERS/FAERS damage may slow prescriber adoption for years. Early-adopter\u2192mainstream transition is stalled for VYKAT.\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIO ENGINE (Bayesian)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior (Layer 1.5) updated with (a) 2026 guidance raise [Actual], (b) STAT safety report [Actual], (c) NBI-827104 Phase 2 failure [Actual \u2014 NeurologyLive], (d) 2027 readouts pending.\n\n| Scenario | Prob | Description | Value/sh | 50%/80% CI |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Bull | 25% | Both 2027 Phase 3s succeed; INGREZZA holds to 2036; VYKAT contained; CRENESSITY $1.8B | $200 | 50% CI $95\u2013160; 80% CI $70\u2013205 |\n| Base | 50% | Commercial anchor only; LOE onset 2031\u201332; VYKAT restricted growth | $113 | |\n| Bear | 20% | One Phase 3 fails; LOE 2030; VYKAT withdrawal (overlay) | $75 | |\n| Severe | 5% | VYKAT withdrawn + INGREZZA accelerated generic erosion + CRENESSITY plateau | $50 | |\n\n**Expected value = 0.25\u00d7200 + 0.50\u00d7113 + 0.20\u00d775 + 0.05\u00d750 = $124** [Arithmetic]\n**Margin of safety = (113 \u2212 152.57)/113 = \u221235%** [Arithmetic] \u2192 **None.**\nExpected 12-month return (EV vs price) = \u221218.7% [Arithmetic].\n\nSECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket horizon implied at $152.57 \u2248 6\u20138 years of double-digit growth and \u226550% pipeline success [Assumption]. My forecast horizon: 7 years explicit, base-case pipeline only in overlay. **Spread = 0\u20132 years \u2014 no arbitrage available at T0.** Arbitrage would open at \u2264$118 (base MoS \u2265 15%).\n\nSECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u