 accruals ratio -0.073 [Arithmetic] supports cash quality. Main risk is product-concentration.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard\n- Revenue Growth (3-yr CAGR FY22-FY25): 24.3% [Arithmetic]\n- Operating Margin FY2025: 21.6% [Filed] | TTM: ~21.4% [Arithmetic]\n- ROE: 22.1% (vendor) [Estimate]\n- FCF Margin (TTM): 25.8% [Arithmetic]\n- FCF / Net Income: 1.23x [Arithmetic]\n- Net Debt: Net cash ~$67M using vendor total debt $0.415B and Q2'26 cash+securities $0.482B [Estimate] \u2014 but debt components unresolved [Unconfirmed]\n- Interest Coverage: extremely high; interest expense immaterial [Actual]\n- Judgment: EXCELLENT\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard\n1. Buyback efficiency: 1/3 (slight net buyback 1yr, 2.9% 3-yr dilution)\n2. M&A track record: 1/3 (Soleno unproven; no multi-cycle record)\n3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 (low capex, high incremental ROIC)\n4. Rationality of mix: 2/3 (high R&D reinvestment; some empire risk)\n5. Guidance accuracy: 2/3 (raised INGREZZA guidance; prior-year beat pattern)\nInsider bonus: 0 \u2014 insider ownership 1.06%; no cluster buy [Aggregator]\nTotal: 9/15 \u2192 GOOD\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization (4-year straight-line amortization)\n- FY2025 R&D (derived): ~$1.026B [Estimate \u2014 Revenue - COGS estimate - SG&A - OI]\n- R&D amortization (4-yr avg of FY22-FY25): ~$0.730B [Estimate]\n- Adjusted Operating Income = $0.619B + $1.026B - $0.730B = $0.915B [Estimate]\n- Unamortized R&D at FY2025: ~$1.31B [Estimate]\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC Treatment\n- FY2025 SBC: $0.218B [Filed]\n- Adjusted FCF = Reported FCF $0.749B - SBC $0.218B = $0.531B [Arithmetic]\n- This adjusted FCF is the correct owner-cash baseline for DCF.\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization\n- FY2025 operating leases: $0.471B [Filed] \u2014 not added to net debt in core DCF to avoid double-counting rent in EBIT; flagged as off-balance sheet.\n\nStep 2.5-4. Adjusted ROIC\n- Adjusted Invested Capital = Equity $3.253B + Debt $0.415B + Leases $0.471B + Unamortized R&D $1.31B - Cash & Investments $2.543B = $2.906B [Estimate]\n- Adjusted ROIC = $0.915B \u00d7 (1-0.21) / $2.906B = 24.9% [Estimate]\n- GAAP ROIC is distorted by large cash/investment balances; adjusted ROIC is the more credible economic number.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett style, FY2025)\n- Net income $0.479B + D&A $0.030B - maintenance capex $0.034B - \u0394 non-cash WC ~$0.000B = $0.475B [Estimate]\n- Owner earnings per share = $4.68 [Estimate]\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550