o: INGREZZA (valbenazine \u2014 tardive dyskinesia and Huntington's chorea), CRENESSITY (crinecerfont \u2014 classic congenital adrenal hyperplasia), VYKAT XR (diazoxide choline \u2014 Prader-Willi hyperphagia, acquired with Soleno, May 2026). Pipeline: late-stage osavampator (MDD) and direclidine (schizophrenia) with Phase 3 readouts in 2027. **Understandability: High.**\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat assessment (0\u20133 each):**\n| Moat type | Score | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, patents, IP to 2036\u20132038+) | 3 | Stable/Widening |\n| Switching costs (stabilized patients, physician inertia) | 3 | Stable |\n| Network effects | 0 | \u2014 |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Stable |\n| Economies of scale (specialty sales force) | 2 | Widening |\n| Regulatory/orphan barriers | 3 | Stable |\n| Data moat (real-world safety/efficacy) | 2 | Narrowing for VYKAT; Widening elsewhere |\n| **Total** | **14 / 21** | **Wide moat** \u2014 but VYKAT's safety signal [Actual \u2014 STAT] is narrowing one franchise |\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch classification:** **Fast grower** (3-yr revenue CAGR +22.3% [Actual]). Checkpoint: growth durability hinges on INGREZZA LOE timing [Unconfirmed] \u2014 the core risk.\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial strength scorecard:**\n- Revenue CAGR 5-yr: +22.3% [Actual]; Revenue 3-yr CAGR: ~+16.6% [Arithmetic on FY22\u201325]\n- Operating margin: TTM 21.6%; 11-yr median 9.2% [Actual] \u2192 expanding\n- ROE: 22.1% [Vendor \u2014 Actual]; ROIC est. \u226514% [Assumption]\n- FCF conversion: OCF/NI = 1.27 TTM [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt: cash+marketable securities $482M (6/30/2026) vs operating leases $471M (FY25) \u2192 \u2248 net neutral; $1.0B revolver undrawn [Actual \u2014 company]\n- **Judgment: Excellent** quantitative scorecard; SBC drag is the main quality discount.\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u20133 each):**\nBuyback efficiency 2 (net buyback 2025 but modest); M&A track record 1 (Soleno $2.9B all-cash for a safety-flagged asset [Actual