t Option-Led overlay**. The commercial franchise is profitable and FCF-generative (anchors Engine 1); the 2027 Phase 3 readouts add genuine option value (Engine 4 overlay). Transition evidence: commercial portfolio now 3 products; 2026 revenue \u2248 $3.9B with 3 launches; but pipeline is not yet revenue >50% or FCF-positive on its own. Per 0-3, **Blended Engine = Engine 1 (65%) + Engine 4 (35%)** weighted. If a single engine were forced, Engine 1.\n\n**Forecast \u2014 explicit per-year model (all dollars in $B except per-share):**\n\n| Year | Revenue | EBIT margin | EBIT | nOPAT (21%) | +D&A | \u2212SBC | \u2212Capex | \u2212\u0394WC | FCF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 3.87 | 32.0% | 1.238 | 0.978 | 0.115 | 0.260 | 0.040 | 0.053 | **0.740** |\n| 2027 | 4.42 | 33.5% | 1.481 | 1.170 | 0.120 | 0.290 | 0.050 | 0.028 | **0.922** |\n| 2028 | 4.80 | 34.5% | 1.656 | 1.308 | 0.125 | 0.320 | 0.055 | 0.019 | **1.039** |\n| 2029 | 5.05 | 34.5% | 1.742 | 1.376 | 0.125 | 0.340 | 0.060 | 0.013 | **1.088** |\n| 2030 | 5.00 | 33.0% | 1.650 | 1.304 | 0.130 | 0.340 | 0.060 | (0.003) | **1.037** |\n| 2031 | 4.85 | 30.0% | 1.455 | 1.149 | 0.120 | 0.330 | 0.060 | (0.008) | **0.887** |\n| 2032 | 4.60 | 27.0% | 1.242 | 0.981 | 0.115 | 0.320 | 0.060 | (0.013) | **0.729** |\n| Terminal | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | **0.620** |\n\n**Revenue path (sourced):**\n- INGREZZA: FY25 $2.5B [Actual]; 2026 guided $2.825\u20132.875B [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 release]; 2027 +10%, 2028 +5%, 2029 0%, 2030 \u22125%, 2031\u221232 \u221210%/yr [Assumption \u2014 LOE onset modeled 2031\u201332; patents to 2036 [Unconfirmed], Paragraph IV open since 2025 [Unconfirmed] creates wide uncertainty]\n- CRENESSITY: FY25 $301M [Actual]; 2026 \u2248 $0.74B [Estimate \u2014 Q1 $153M + Q2 $184M + H2; [Actual quarters]]; to $1.6B by 2030 [Assumption \u2014 orphan ramp, IP to 2038 [Actual]]\n- VYKAT XR: 2026 \u2248 $0.25B [Estimate \u2014 $54M partial Q2 + full Q3/Q4 [Actual]; pro-forma $94M/quarter [Actual]]; 2027\u20132030 $0.30\u2192$0.22B [Assumption \u2014 safety-driven deceleration: 7 deaths/100+ SAEs [Actual \u2014 STAT]]\n- Other revenue: ~$0.02B/yr [Actual history]\n\n**Margin path (sourced):** 2026 non-GAAP R&D guide $1.14\u20131.19B; non-GAAP SG&A $1.325\u20131.35B [Actual] \u2192 non-GAAP EBIT \u2248 32% in 2026; expansion to 34.5% by 2029 on operating leverage [Assumption]; contraction 2030\u201332 as INGREZZA erodes [Assumption].\n**SBC:** $218M FY25 [Actual]; $260M FY26 (incl. ~$58M Soleno acceleration [Actual]); ~7% of revenue thereafter [Assumption]. **Treated as cash expense \u2014 deliberate; the pack's warning on OCF-minus-SBC is followed.**\n**Capex:** $34M FY25 [Actual]; $40\u201360M thereafter [Assumption \u2014 asset-light, 1.2% of revenue].\n**\u0394WC:** non-cash WC at ~5% of incremental revenue; releases in decline years [Assumption].\n**D&A:** $30M FY25 + $85\u201390M acquired-intangible amortization 2026 [Actual] \u2192 $115M, rising to $130M [Assumption].\n**Tax rate:** 21% US statutory [Assumption \u2014 pack notes rate not held but identity holds].\n**Discount rate (WACC):** Rf = 4.7% [Actual \u2014 10Y 2026-08-21]; ERP = 4.5% [Assumption]; beta = 0.65 [Assumption \u2014 vendor beta 0.394 is window-unreliable, [Actual-tagged but not consumption-grade]; 0.65 reflects clinical-event idiosyncratic risk]; **CoE = 4.7% + 0.65\u00d74.5% = 7.6%; no debt \u2192 WACC = 7.6%; round to 8.0%** [Assumption \u2014 small-cap/pipeline premium].\n\n**DCF output at 8.0%:**\nExplicit FCF PV (2026\u20132032): $4.79B [Arithmetic]\nTerminal value: $0.620/0.08 = $7.75B; PV = $4.52B [Arithmetic]\nEV = $9.31B; + net cash \u2248 $0.01B (cash+securities $482M post-Soleno [Actual] \u2212 op leases $471M [Actual]; investment-overlap [Unconfirmed])\n**Equity value = $9.32B \u2192 $91.7/share (commercial core, no pipeline).**\n**Pipeline option overlay (Engine 4):** osavampator 50% success \u00d7 $1.0B peak PV \u2248 $0.9B; direclidine 35% \u00d7 $1.5B peak PV \u2248 $1.0B; early pipeline \u2248 $0.2B [All Assumption/Estimate \u2014 weighted for 2028\u201329 launch] \u2192 +$2.1B \u2248 **+$21/share.**\n**\u2192 Intrinsic value, base, pipeline-inclusive: \u2248 $113/share.**\nSensitivity (commercial core): WACC 7% \u2192 +$13/sh; WACC 9% \u2192 \u2212$11/sh; terminal g = 2% \u2192 +$6\u201312/sh; INGREZZA LOE pushed to 2036 \u2192 +$3\u20135/sh.\n\n**Multiples cross-check:** 2027 consensus non-GAAP EPS $10.79 [Estimate \u2014 Zacks]; restoring SBC (~$2.7/sh) \u2192 real EPS \u2248 $8.1 \u2192 at 14\u201315x = $113\u2013121 [Estimate]. Trailing GAAP P/E 22.0x [Vendor]; forward 2026 GAAP EPS \u2248 $5.4 [Assumption] \u2192 28x. EV/EBITDA(2026E) \u2248 15.5/1.355 = 11.4x [Arithmetic]. **Cross-check corroborates $113\u2013125, not $153.**\n**Reverse DCF at T0 $152.57:** requires 2030 revenue \u2248 $7\u20138B with two pipeline approvals and INGREZZA holding to 2036, or WACC \u22646.5%. That is bull-case, not base-case [Assumption].\n**Tornado (top-3 drivers):** (1) INGREZZA LOE timing; (2) VYKAT regulatory outcome; (3) 2027 Phase 3 results.\n\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- **Competitive response:** INGREZZA \u2013 3\u20134 generic filers after 2025 Paragraph IV [Unconfirmed] and 2 other VMAT2 franchises (Austedo) \u2192 price competition post-LOE severe. CRENESSITY \u2013 no near-term competitor; in-licensed alternatives historically failed. VYKAT \u2013 no competitor in PWS hyperphagia, but safety scrutiny suppresses the category. Impact: \u22121 (net).\n- **Reflexivity:** Positive \u2014 strong stock enabled the $2.9B all-cash Soleno deal [Actual]; negative \u2014 a derating would impair M&A currency and SBC attractiveness. Feedback loop real but secondary.\n- **Customer/LTV evolution:** INGREZZA prescriber base mature; CRENESSITY extends from adults to pediatric and now <4yr Phase 2 (initiated [Actual]); VYKAT's VAERS/FAERS damage may slow prescriber adoption for years. Early-adopter\u2192mainstream transition is stalled for VYKAT.\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIO ENGINE (Bayesian)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior (Layer 1.5) updated with (a) 2026 guidance raise [Actual], (b) STAT safety report [Actual], (c) NBI-827104 Phase 2 failure [Actual \u2014 NeurologyLive], (d) 2027 readouts pending.\n\n| Scenario | Prob | Description | Value/sh | 50%/80% CI |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Bull | 25% | Both 2027 Phase 3s succeed; INGREZZA holds to 2036; VYKAT contained; CRENESSITY $1.8B | $200 | 50% CI $95\u2013160; 80% CI $70\u2013205 |\n| Base | 50% | Commercial anchor only; LOE onset 2031\u201332; VYKAT restricted growth | $113 | |\n| Bear | 20% | One Phase 3 fails; LOE 2030; VYKAT withdrawal (overlay) | $75 | |\n| Severe | 5% | VYKAT withdrawn + INGREZZA accelerated generic erosion + CRENESSITY plateau | $50 | |\n\n**Expected value = 0.25\u00d7200 + 0.50\u00d7113 + 0.20\u00d775 + 0.05\u00d750 = $124** [Arithmetic]\n**Margin of safety = (113 \u2212 152.57)/113 = \u221235%** [Arithmetic] \u2192 **None.**\nExpected 12-month return (EV vs price) = \u221218.7% [Arithmetic].\n\nSECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket horizon implied at $152.57 \u2248 6\u20138 years of double-digit growth and \u226550% pipeline success [Assumption]. My forecast horizon: 7 years explicit, base-case pipeline only in overlay. **Spread = 0\u20132 years \u2014 no arbitrage available at T0.** Arbitrage would open at \u2264$118 (base MoS \u2265 15%).\n\nSECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Conviction score (15):** Business quality 4; Valuation attractiveness 1 (\u221235% MoS); Macro alignment 2 (mild headwind); Thesis clarity 4 (INGREZZA TRx, CRENESSITY reimbursement, VYKAT FAERS, 2027 readouts); Execution traceability 4 (guidance discipline). **Total = 11/15 \u2192 High conviction on the business; Low conviction on the price.**\nConviction decay: \u22121/6 months unless catalysts confirm.\n**Sizing:** Max weight for High conviction = 4\u20136%; at negative MoS, new money = 0%; held = trim to \u22644%.\n\nSECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- Short interest: 5.61% of float; DTC 3.4 days; MoM \u221220.6% [Vendor \u2014 2026-08-13] \u2192 moderate, declining; no squeeze setup.\n- Institutional ownership 105.84% [Vendor] (double-counted in 13F) \u2192 crowded; ETF-flow vulnerability in a derating.\n- Insider: 1.06% [Vendor] \u2014 neutral; no cluster buys.\n- Options/sentiment: not held [Unconfirmed]; sell-side mean PT $211.57 vs price $152.57 \u2192 positive bias still present; stock is 18% off the $186.12 high after the STAT safety article [Actual].\n- **Crowding risk: 7/15** \u2014 position-size haircut \u22121%p if held.\n\nSECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nLow macro beta (0.394 vendor [Unconfirmed window]); healthcare/defensive cash flows; idiosyncratic drivers (FDA, Phase 3 data, LOE). Portfolio-role: growth-with-defensive-tilt satellite. At 0% new money, no contribution. If held, cap at 4% given negative MoS.\n\nSECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nEV = $124 vs price $152.57: edge = \u221218.7% \u2192 **Kelly = 0%**. Breakeven: $124. Entry zones: $118 \u2192 Kelly \u2248 +1%; $110 \u2192 Kelly \u2248 +4.5%; $100 \u2192 Kelly \u2248 +8%. **Layer 5 (0%) vs Layer 6.5 (0%) gap = 0%p \u2014 consistent; no re-analysis needed.**\n\nSECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Catalysts (12\u201324 mo):** 2027 Phase 3 readouts (osavampator/MDD, direclidine/schizophrenia) [Actual]; CRENESSITY pediatric label expansion; INGREZZA litigation/settlement resolution [Unconfirmed]; VYKAT safety review outcome [Unconfirmed].\n**Risks:** VYKAT restriction/withdrawal (7 deaths, 100+ SAEs \u2014 STAT [Actual]); INGREZZA LOE 2031\u201336; SBC dilution; M&A integration; pricing legislation; cash drawdown to $482M \u2014 still adequate with $1.0B revolver [Actual].\n\nSECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nNBIX's common bear triggers: (i) rates-up-groth-multiple-compression; (ii) biotech-sector risk-off; (iii) idiosyncratic FDA. Portfolio stress: 2022-type growth derating would hit NBIX with the sector despite low beta. Conditional VaR contribution: ~6\u20139% loss in a 2\u03c3 market stress [Assumption]. Tail-correlation with S&P: 0.4\u20130.5 (regime-dependent) [Unconfirmed].\n\nSECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nThesis-integrity thresholds (quarterly check):\n1. INGREZZA TRx growth \u22658% YoY; if <5% for two consecutive quarters \u2192 reassess LOE/timing thesis.\n2. CRENESSITY quarterly net sales \u2265$160M; reimbursement \u226580%; if reimbursement slips \u2192 reassess peak.\n3. VYKAT: monitor FDA adverse-event reports; any additional deaths or FDA/EMA regulatory action \u2192 cut position by half immediately.\n4. Operating margin (non-GAAP) \u226530%; if <27% for two quarters \u2192 thesis damaged.\n5. Cash+securities + revolver \u2265$1.0B; if <$0.5B and no financing \u2192 distress flag.\n6. 2027 Phase 3: osavampator and direclidine primary endpoints \u2014 binary re-pricing events; position sized accordingly.\n\nSECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM / ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Short thesis bullets:**\n1. VYKAT: FAERS shows 7 deaths, 100+ SAEs \u2014 40\u201360% chance of label restriction or withdrawal [Unconfirmed]; $2.9B acquisition value impaired.\n2. INGREZZA = 73% of 2026 revenue; LOE 2031\u201336 with Paragraph IV already filed; generic erosion of 60\u201380% is a 30\u201350% base-rate event [Unconfirmed].\n3. SBC $218M/yr \u2248 30% of net income \u2014 real economic cost per the pack's own instruction.\n4. Non-GAAP EPS ($9.47 2026E) adds back SBC, acquisition costs, amortization \u2014 GAAP EPS \u2248 $5.4 \u2192 stock at 28x GAAP, not 16x.\n5. Full GAAP R&D (2026E $1.3B) yields only one Phase 2 failure (NBI-827104) so far \u2014 no de-risked asset in late-stage.\n6. M&A discipline: Soleno was all-cash, fully-priced, and safety-flagged within 3 months of close \u2014 a warning on management judgment.\n7. At $152.57, the market pays for 2 successful Phase 3 launches at 50%+ probability each \u2014 above CNS base rates.\n\n**Logic combat:** Long 6.5/10 vs Short 7/10 at T0 \u2014 **gap <2 \u2192 conviction downgrade by one step.** (The short case is stronger only at this price; the business itself is good.)\n\nSECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- Methodology: 37-point audit. Pass 34/37. Failures: (i) no quarterly segment margins \u2014 SOTP disabled; (ii) net-cash exactness unresolved (investment overlap); (iii) 2027 consensus not pinned to a dated quarter in the pack. \n- Bias audit: the SBC-as-cash stance is deliberately conservative; the VYKAT safety overlay may be too harsh (drug is first-and-only for a lethal disease \u2014 FDA historically retains). A 15% withdrawal overlay remains in the Bear scenario only.\n- Consistency: FY26 revenue +35% consistent with TTM +34%; margins consistent with non-GAAP guidance; FCF bridge consistent with OCF\u2212SBC\u2212capex.\n- Red-team audit: passed \u2014 short thesis is fully articulated.\n- **Data integrity:** vendor beta window unstated; short data semimonthly; net-cash overlap [Unconfirmed] \u2014 all flagged. Conclusion: conclusions do not depend on any single disputed number (sensitivity: \u00b110% from net-cash ambiguity alone).\n\nSECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDate: 2026-08-24 | T0: $152.57 | IV: $113 (50% CI 95\u2013135) | EV: $124 | Action: No new position / trim to \u22644%\nKey assumptions logged: INGREZZA LOE onset 2031; VYKAT decelerated not withdrawn in base; both Phase 3s absent from base; SBC expensed; WACC 8%. Red-team concern overrides: FAERS deaths + all-cash Soleno + crowded ownership.\n\nSECTION 12 \u2014 FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Action: DO NOT INITIATE \u2014 AVOID at T0 $152.57. If held, TRIM to \u22644% weight.**\n**Conviction:** High on business quality; Low on entry valuation.\n**Weight:** 0% new money; \u22644% if inherited.\n**Strategy /**\n- Entry zone: $100\u2013118 (where MoS \u226515% and Kelly \u22652\u20135%). Limit ladder: \u2153 at $118, \u2153 at $110, \u2153 at $100.\n- Re-entry trigger without a pullback: positive 2027 Phase 3 readouts for either program, or INGREZZA settlement that pushes LOE to \u22652035, with price \u2264$170.\n- Exit/redemption triggers: any additional VYKAT deaths or FDA restriction; INGREZZA litigation loss; two consecutive quarters of INGREZZA TRx <5% YoY.\n- Expected 12-month return at T0: **\u2248 \u221219%** (EV $124 vs price $152.57).\n\n**Bottom line:** NBIX is a high-quality, wide-moat franchise compounding through INGREZZA, CRENESSITY and a deep pipeline \u2014 but at $152.57 the market capitalizes non-GAAP earnings that do not exist on a GAAP basis, fully prices the 2027 pipeline at success, and discounts the VYKAT safety signal. The price is 35% above intrinsic value and 19% above probability-weighted value. **Discipline says wait.**\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n```"}], "arm": "cloud_api", "model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "research_brief_age_days": 18.6}
